# Review package: batch 9, slice journal

## 2df69d65 Journal every change and commit it only under a lease the keeper holds

Every row change in public now writes a row to net.journal in the same transaction, and a deferred constraint trigger on
that table asks net.assert_lease at commit, so a machine without a lease commits nothing (fence 1). migrateDb takes the
journal off before the migrations and puts it back after, also after a failed run, because each table's journal function
names its columns and a migration that drops one and writes that table would otherwise fail. Foreign keys become
deferrable after every run, so a later migration's new key is too. public.applied, public.tool_calls and task_events.uuid
come with it, and both new tables are closed to the agent roles.

Superusers that do not say hornhoof.fenced = on pass, so plan 2's build, migrate and an owner's psql keep writing. Agent
roles are fenced whatever they set. The whole PGlite suite now runs fenced under an endless lease.

Migrations are 0056_sources and 0057_net by build ruling 5, and the plan's tests read so (0044_link_tls is 0055_link_tls).
Proved by test/journal.test.ts, migrations.test.ts, orchestrator-control.test.ts and test/real/journal.test.ts. The real
tests were also seen red against code with the fence off, the detach off and the put-back off, each for its own reason.

Ruling: tasks_turn_id and tasks_product_id not added and their test not repeated - why: both are already in schema.ts and 0045_task_lookup_indexes, and migrations.test.ts "creates both indexes on a fresh install" makes the same pg_indexes check - cost if wrong: none, the check stays.
Ruling: added net.write_journal, net.pair_for_journal and net.source_of_journal beyond the plan's list - why: one place makes a journal row and small functions build each table's body; their names do not start with journal_, so detach_journal leaves them - cost if wrong: plan 3 Task 4's problems() sees three more functions of net, all revoked from PUBLIC.
Ruling: hasCode added to db/errors.ts, a file the task does not list - why: isLeaseRefused would otherwise repeat isUniqueViolation's walk over causes - cost if wrong: none, its behaviour is pinned by the existing tests.
Ruling: an update's key is the new row's key - why: the plan does not say which; a changed primary key column still shows in cols and old - cost if wrong: plan 8's merge reads the old key from old in that rare case.
Ruling: attach_journal answers how many triggers it newly attached, so 0 on a second run - why: the plan says how many tables it attached - cost if wrong: nothing reads the number yet.
Ruling: a json column is not handled, since IS DISTINCT FROM has no equality for it - why: the schema has only jsonb, smallest edit - cost if wrong: a later migration adding json fails the first update of that table, which the fenced suite shows at once.
Ruling: added two tests beyond the plan's list, no lease or state row refuses and a table without a key or with a long name raises - why: both are fail closed behaviour the plan requires and a fresh install starts with no rows - cost if wrong: about 3 s of test time.

